oth rules at Build AND Decode. `checkPayload` runs `decodeStrictObject` on the top-level frame only and, for the 24 non-message-like kinds, validates only `content_blocks` when present; the payload then enters through lenient `json.Unmarshal` (float64, last-duplicate-wins) and is sealed by `canonicalizeObject`. Witnessed through the production entries for `usage`, `tool_call`, `opaque_event` and `error`: `{\"n\":9007199254740993}` is ADMITTED and sealed as `9007199254740992` — rounded and continued, which Section 1.6 forbids outright and which fixture NUM-UNSAFE-ROUND names as nonconforming; `2^60` seals as `1152921504606847000`; `{\"facts\":{\"a\":1,\"a\":2}}` seals as `{\"facts\":{\"a\":2}}`; `{\"n\":1.5}` and `{\"n\":1e2}` seal as-is; `DecodeCanonicalEvent` admits every one of them resealed. The omit-self identity of a Canonical Event is therefore computed over rounded or collapsed bytes. Fix: validate non-message payload values — number model, nested duplicates, at depth — at Build and at Decode with the walker you already wrote; add negatives at BOTH entries for a non-message kind; assert the SEALED BYTES are never rounded or collapsed (not merely that the call refuses); ship a narrowing mutant.\n5|P2-α — the new extension-value gate is measured at 2 of its 17 admission sites: per-site narrowing plants survive the whole suite at 15 sites, twice. Add one extension value-fault negative per admission site (the 16 Decode sites plus the two payload-level sites) and the matching harness rows. A gate wired at 17 sites and tested at 2 is the same \"gate wired, evidence missing\" shape the previous round already asked you to close.\n6|P2-β — `decodeRawEntries` (rawmanifest.go:389) admits an equal-key duplicate entry at Decode under a `<=`→`<` narrowing with the whole suite green, twice. Add the decode duplicate-entry row and its harness row.\n7|P2-γ — `checkPlanItemMatch` (your P3-c fix) is defeated by duplicate plan keys: `plan=[a,a,token]` with items `[a,b,token]` seals a manifest carrying an item that is not a plan candidate. Refuse duplicate plan keys there; negative plus narrowing mutant. Note the shape: the same duplicate-defeats-the-count bug you fixed in `deriveRawComplete` last round exists in the sibling you added to fix a different finding — when you fix a counting rule, check every other place that counts.\n8|P3 — work the reviewer's list: the null-content XOR; the three misreporting messages; rows for `input_blocked`, `-(2^53)`, U+2029, a payload top-level duplicate and the decode external-null-parent; the `EncodeNativeIdentity` contract; the `N-main-count` note; the dead `sourceBasisObject`; and either state or cover the census arms it names. Each one is named with its probe in the verdict.\n9|Procedure: TRUNK HAS MOVED. origin/main is now 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91 and carries the v0.7.0 adoption (PR #52): internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md, internal/specpin/v0.7.0.lock.json, internal/catalog/catalog.v0.7.0.json with `catalog.Adopted = ReleaseV070`, internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json. Your candidate sits on base 888ae3d. Run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-24z2b3` FIRST, then audit every path in `git diff --name-only 888ae3d 2fc6d50` that also appears in your `git status` — README.md and LOGBOOK.md both moved on trunk with that landing, so your edits must be purely additive on top of the NEW content and must never restore the old bytes; task-board.config.json must end byte-identical to the new base. You are a FIRST leaf: do NOT touch internal/traceability (the final leaf TASK-260830-32ypr2 carries the registry bindings and the pin). Once refreshed, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the full configured 27-command validation suite once (command 5 `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs — expected, do not shorten it), update TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__), reset and re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-24z2b3 --role developer` so revision 4 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 3.5 hours in.\n10|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: this task has already lost a run to a provider \"model stream idle timeout\" (the runtime cancels it and spawns a successor that re-reads this brief from the start). The Story worktree is NOT reset when that happens — it still carries whatever the dead attempt wrote. Before anything else run `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, write into your results exactly what was already present when you started, and verify every pre-existing change against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n11|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 4.","final_result":true}}}
