iteral at or beyond 2^53 … \n95|Implementations MUST NOT round a value and continue\"; fixture NUM-UNSAFE-ROUND\n96|names exactly the behaviour witnessed (\"an implementation that first rounds it\n97|to 9007199254740992 is nonconforming\"). This is the P1-b mechanism at a\n98|different member: the omit-self identity of a Canonical Event 1.0.0 is sealed\n99|over rounded or collapsed bytes. TRACEABILITY.md states \"per-kind fact values\n100|(including their numbers) are the normalization sibling's registry\"; that bound\n101|covers WHICH facts a kind may carry (\"Payloads contain only their registered\n102|typed facts\"), not the §1.6 value model, which governs every member of every\n103|1.0.0 object and which this leaf's own `checkPayload` is the only gate for — a\n104|sibling registry cannot un-round what `BuildCanonicalEvent` has already sealed,\n105|and `opaque_event` payloads have no registry at all. Message-like payloads are\n106|closed (P2w/P2v rows: block and payload `extensions` refuse `1.5`/`2^53`).\n107|\n108|Fix: walk the payload object with the existing `checkExtensionValues` walker\n109|(it already accepts any object and enforces integer literals, |n| ≤ 2^53−1, no\n110|fraction/exponent, duplicate-free nested objects, depth bound) at Build and\n111|Decode for every kind, or decode the payload with `UseNumber` and validate\n112|before sealing; negatives for `1.5`, `2^53`, `2^53+1` (assert the sealed bytes\n113|are never produced), a nested duplicate, at both entries for a non-message\n114|kind; a narrowing mutant (admit exactly `2^53` in payloads).\n115|\n116|### P2-α — The extension-value gate is measured at 2 of 17 sites\n117|\n118|`checkExtensionsClosed` is called at 16 Decode admission sites plus the shared\n119|Build helper `encodeExtensions`. A per-site narrowing that keeps the key check\n120|and drops the value model at ONE site (`site_plants.py`, whole suite as killer,\n121|2 runs each, `logs/mutants/S-ext-values-*`):\n122|\n123|| Site | Verdict |\n124||---|---|\n125|| `rawmanifest.go:319` (raw manifest decode), `rawmanifest.go:483` (`encodeExtensions`, all Build entries) | KILLED 2/2 |\n126|| `boundary.go:90` ax basis, `:116` external basis, `:331` stable proof, `:428` stable boundary, `:465` unstable boundary; `capturebuild.go:308` capture manifest; `captureitem.go:143` capture item; `event.go:297` source evidence, `:558` event, `:603` message payload, `:675` content block; `identity.go:112` native identity, `:233` workspace binding; `session.go:94` actor, `:454` session | **SURVIVED 2/2** (15 sites) |\n127|\n128|The arms all work (P2w rows all REFUSED), so this is missing evidence, not\n129|broken code — the same shape as rev2 P2-b for the new gate. The conformance\n130|matrix cites one test (`TestRawManifestRefusals/extension_values`) for the\n131|whole rule and the refusal census confirms the 14 Decode `extensions %s` sites\n132|are uncovered. Fix (test-only): one value-fault row per admission site — a\n133|table over every Decode entry injecting `1.5` (or `2^53`) into that shape's\n134|`extensions`, plus the two payload-level sites — and a harness row per site or\n135|a per-site loop.\n136|\n137|### P2-β — `decodeRawEntries` equal-key duplicate at Decode is unmeasured (`rawmanifest.go:389`)\n138|\n139|`R3-raw-entries-dup-decode` (`key <= previous` → `key < previous` at the Decode\n140|site only) SURVIVED the whole suite 2/2 (`logs/mutants/R3-raw-entries-dup-decode-run{1,2}.log`)\n141|and SURVIVED `-run TestRawManifestRefusals/decode`. The decode table has\n142|\"unsorted entries\" (a swap) but no equal-key duplicate row; the producer's\n143|`N-raw-order` mutates only the Build site. Same class as rev2 P2-b (the capture\n144|items got their decode duplicate row in rev3; the raw entries did not). Fix\n145|(test-only): a decode duplicate-entry row + harness row.\n146|\n147|### P2-γ — Duplicate plan keys defeat the one-per-plan-candidate rule at Build (`capturebuild.go:361-375`)\n148|\n149|`checkPlanItemMatch` compares `len(items)` with `len(planKeys)` and then checks\n150|plan→item membership only, so a repeated plan key hides an unplanned item.\n151|Probe P5c: `PlanKeys=[store/blob-a, store/blob-a, store/token-cache]`,\n152|`Items=[store/blob-a, store/blob-b, store/token-cache]` → `BuildCaptureManifest`\n153|ADMITTED and sealed (`raw_complete=false`, 3 items) although `store/blob-b` is\n154|not a plan candidate — exactly the object P3-c was fixed to refuse. This is the\n155|P2-d asymmetry one level up (the \"no extra\" half is defeated by a duplicate the\n156|way the \"all\" half of `deriveRawComplete` was). The capture-plan sink is\n157|\"sorted unique CapturePlanItem\" (§7.8), so duplicate plan keys are malformed\n158|input that Build must refuse, not seal. Fix: refuse duplicate `PlanKeys` in\n159|`checkPlanItemMatch` (and/or check item→plan membership); negative + narrowing\n160|mutant. `VerifyCaptureReconciliation` is not affected (P4f/P4g: duplicate plan\n161|keys derive false and are refused).\n162|\n163|### P3 — bounds, precision, hygiene\n164|\n165|- P3-a′ **Content block `content: null` passes the XOR** (`event.go:650-663`):\n166|  `hasContent` is member presence, and `rawString(null)` succeeds with `\"\"`,\n167|  so `{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":null}` is ADMITTED (probe P7d) while\n168|  `blob_descriptor_id: null` is REFUSED (P7e). Make the XOR a non-null test.\n169|- P3-b′ **Refusal detail misreports value faults** at `captureitem.go:144`,\n170|  `session.go:95`, `event.go:676`: every extension fault (number, nested\n171|  duplicate, depth) is reported as \"are not reverse-DNS keyed\" (P2w rows\n172|  `items[0].extensions 1.5`, `actors[0].extensions 1.5`,\n173|  `content_blocks[0].extensions 1.5`). Use `%s` with the fault like the other\n174|  13 sites.\n175|- P3-c′ **Unmeasured arms found by narrowing** (each SURVIVED 2/2, whole\n176|  suite; the arms themselves work per probe): the `input_blocked` boolean of\n177|  the closed_store/provider_quiescence coupling (`R3-proof-input-blocked`;\n178|  probe P20c refuses; only foreground/background idle have rows); the negative\n179|  edge `-(2^53)` of `checkAXNumberLiteral` (`R3-ax-number-negative-edge`;\n180|  probe refuses); the Zp arm (U+2029) of the sanitizer (`R3-sanitizer-zp`;\n181|  corpus pins Zl U+2028 and Cf only); the payload top-level duplicate refusal\n182|  (`R3-payload-strict-object`; probe N3e refuses); the decode-side external\n183|  actor with null parent (`R3-decode-external-null-parent`; decode rows use a\n184|  subagent only). Informational, not defects: U+009F (C1 class pinned by\n185|  U+0085), the fraction arm of `checkAXNumberLiteral` (subsumed by\n186|  `ParseInt`), the 256-depth bound moved by one.\n187|- P3-d′ **`EncodeNativeIdentity` (exported) rounds** unsafe extension values:\n188|  `EncodeNativeIdentity(identity, {\"com.example.n\": 1<<60})` returns bytes\n189|  carrying `1152921504606847000` (probe P2u) while its comment says \"encoding\n190|  never admits what decoding refused\". The two production consumers\n191|  (`IdentityDigest`, `buildCaptureManifest`) re-decode, so no sealed object is\n192|  affected; either validate inside the exported entry or state the\n193|  pre-validated-input contract instead of the false sentence.\n194|- P3-e′ **`N-main-count` note over-claims**: `count=2` patches build AND decode\n195|  but its killer (`build_actors/two_mains`) reaches the build site only. The\n196|  decode site IS pinned (`decode/two_mains` kills my decode-only\n197|  `R3-decode-main-count`), so split the row or fix the note.\n198|- P3-f′ **Dead code**: `sourceBasisObject`, `digestOrEmpty`,\n199|  `digestOrEmptyDigest` (`boundary.go:192-226`) have no caller.\n200|- P3-g′ **Refusal census** (`logs/refusal-census.log`, coverage-driven over\n201|  every `invalid(` site): 366 sites, 181 covered, 185 uncovered (rev2:\n202|  359/156/203). Beyond P2-α, the substantive uncovered arms are: `version is\n203|  not 1.0.0` at capture/session/event decode (only the raw manifest has a\n204|  \"bad version\" row), `items`/`actors`/`entries`/`raw_refs` \"not an array\",\n205|  every count maximum (65536 entries/items/raw_refs, 1024 actors, 128 reason\n206|  codes), the Build-side uint53 overflow arms, `blob descriptor self field is\n207|  %q` and `native key is not valid UTF-8` (probe `\\xff` refuses). State them\n208|  as defense-in-depth or add rows.\n209|\n210|## What is clean (verified, not read)\n211|\n212|1. **Spec fidelity, member level** — the rev2→rev3 delta touches no member\n213|   table or vocabulary (`git diff bee4c807…d5b5b0ee`: only gate wiring,\n214|   wrappers, comments), so the rev2 member-for-member verification of the 16\n215|   closed shapes and 6 vocabularies stands; I re-read §13.14.1 and re-checked\n216|   the rules the rework added against the text: \"typed inline content or Blob\n217|   Descriptor references\" (XOR), \"one per plan candidate\", \"inline content is\n218|   at most 64 KiB\" (bytes — N3c refuses 40,000 chars/80,000 bytes),\n219|   \"Closed-store/provider-quiescence requires all booleans true and null\n220|   snapshot identity; immutable-snapshot/log-prefix requires non-null\n221|   identity\" (P20/P20b/P20c/P21), 0..64 parents (P11i refuses 65), 1..1024\n222|   actors (P12i refuses 1025), `RawObjectEntry` has exactly five members (the\n223|   prose \"and extensions\" is overridden by the closed shape, which the code\n224|   follows).\n225|2. **Row-21 exclusion** — `refuseExcludedMember` is called at all four\n226|   construction/decode paths (`buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries`,\n227|   `buildCaptureItem`, `decodeCaptureItem`); no other entry admits a member\n228|   key. Every handoff class (trust.json, config-binding.json,\n229|   pending-commit.json, credentials/<hex>/private-key.pem, credentials/leaf.pem,\n230|   lock, `.trust-stage-*`, `.custody-stage-*`, `lock-stage-*`, `.bak.N`,\n231|   `.pre-rollback.N`, `.ax-config-*`) plus absolute paths and `..` escapes has\n232|   a constructor negative in both manifests and a decode negative; true\n233|   token-preserving narrowings of both arms KILLED 2/2. The landed matchers\n234|   admit `host-channel\\trust.json`, `HOST-CHANNEL/trust.json`,\n235|   `x/host-channel/trust.json`, `host-channel/TRUST.json` (P3x) — hosttrust's\n236|   anchored STATE_DIR-relative contract, outside this leaf, as in rev2.\n237|3. **provhost bound** — `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`\n238|   PASS on the exact tree (225 production files, 5 session-leaf call sites, 0\n239|   elsewhere; `logs/provhost-census.log`); module-wide grep: non-test\n240|   `VerifyObjectIdentity` callers are only `internal/sessrepo` (5 sites);\n241|   `clonebundle` production calls `CalculateObjectIdentity` ×2 and\n242|   `Canonicalize` ×3 only. The any-claim plant at the link arm\n243|   (`R3-link-any-claim`) is KILLED 2/2; the wrong-claim negatives pin both\n244|   the agreement and the install site (`N-descriptor-claim-agreement`,\n245|   `N-install-site-claim`, `R-install-site-claim` KILLED 2/2).\n246|4. **Blob install** — `InstallRawBlob` delegates to `localstore.PutBlob`:\n247|   short, long, same-length-wrong bytes REFUSED \"declared and staged identity\n248|   differ\" (P14/P14b/P14c); a re-install with different bytes after a correct\n249|   install REFUSED, the same bytes ADMITTED (P14f/P14g — no-replace); a\n250|   descriptor whose `size` disagrees with its chunks is refused by the owner\n251|   before install (P14h); `blob_id != chunk digest` resealed is refused at the\n252|   claim (P14d). Durability bound stated and accurate (no write path in this\n253|   package; `internal/localstore` fault suites green in the four-package run).\n254|   No crash plant of my own: there is no write between which and a receipt\n255|   this package could crash.\n256|5. **Mutation** — producer battery reproduces in the isolated copy: 36 KILLED\n257|   + control SURVIVED, run twice (`logs/mutants-producer-runs1-2.log`, 74 raw\n258|   logs); rev2 re-plants: 19 rows × 2 (`logs/mutants-rev2-replants-runs1-2.log`);\n259|   rev3 plants: 35 rows × 2 + 1 re-plant (`logs/mutants-rev3-runs1-2.log`,\n260|   `…-unstable-explicit-replant.log`): 25 KILLED 2/2, 9 SURVIVED 2/2 (P2-β,\n261|   P3-c′, and the three informational), control SURVIVED 2/2; per-site\n262|   extension plants 17 × 2; per-site wrapper runs 7. The brief's four named\n263|   classes: raw_complete ignoring one unknown item KILLED; always-excluded set\n264|   missing a class KILLED (rev2 machine_auth + producer credential); equal-key\n265|   duplicate at Build KILLED (raw `N-raw-order`, capture\n266|   `R-capture-items-dup-build`) and at Decode KILLED for capture items /\n267|   SURVIVED for raw entries (P2-β); sanitizer admitting one control character\n268|   KILLED for U+001F and U+0085. Every harness restored the tree (diff-clean\n269|   between the two copies after each battery).\n270|6. **Race gate** — see the next section.\n271|7. **Hygiene** — `gofmt -l` empty; `go vet` clean; `go build ./...` OK;\n272|   `go test ./internal/clonebundle ./internal/provhost ./internal/localstore\n273|   ./internal/canonicaljson -count=1` all ok (`logs/four-packages.log`);\n274|   `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` exit 0 (bindings=65,\n275|   clauses 49/535 — unchanged, `internal/traceability` untouched);\n276|   `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit\n277|   0 on the exact tree; `git diff --check` clean; changed paths are exactly\n278|   the 21 candidate paths (nothing outside `internal/clonebundle`, README,\n279|   LOGBOOK; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`); nothing imports `clonebundle`. README\n280|   section has the three test commands and states \"no `ax` command, no\n281|   `doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim\". LOGBOOK entry is\n282|   newest-first under the 2026-09-17 heading. Sibling bounds (per-kind payload\n283|   registries, `maximal_safe` planning, G2 admission, §7.8 wiring, traceability\n284|   re-pin) are stated in doc.go, TRACEABILITY.md, results.md. Package\n285|   coverage 83.9% statements. The conformance matrix's 29 named tests and all\n286|   named call sites exist (owner entries `CheckRequestBody`, `CheckSuccessBody`,\n287|   `CheckFreshSink` in sessadapter; the four\n288|   `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows in canonicaljson).\n289|\n290|## Race gate (item 7)\n291|\n292|The package is untouched by this change: no file outside\n293|`internal/clonebundle`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` changed; `go list -deps` and\n294|`-test -deps ./internal/sessquery` do not include `clonebundle`, and nothing\n295|imports it, so the sessquery race binary is the trunk binary. The rev3 Change\n296|Request validation ran the configured 27-command suite with\n297|`go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` and reports\n298|`required=27 green=27 failed=0 missing=0`; the producer's own cmd05 shows\n299|`ok internal/sessquery 665.226s` under the 25 m timeout. Disposition unchanged\n300|from rev2: a host-capacity artifact, not a candidate defect; the 25 m timeout\n301|landed on trunk (`888ae3d`, TASK-260917-3f8mkd) is the right orchestration\n302|fix, and the honest disclosure was the right call.\n303|\n304|My own measurement (`logs/sessquery-race.log`): `go test ./internal/sessquery\n305|-race -count=1 -timeout 25m` on the pristine candidate copy → `ok … 347.359s`,\n306|wall 349.6 s, exit 0, zero `DATA RACE` lines; host load averages 14.06 → 15.80\n307|over the run with two other `.test` binaries alive at the start (this is a\n308|shared host running other sessions' suites and my own mutation batteries; an\n309|idle host was not available). That is under the old 600 s default even under\n310|that contention; the producer's 665 s was measured while the full 27-command\n311|suite ran concurrently. Two measurements under different load (rev2: 390.6 s\n312|at load 14→10; rev3: 347.4 s at load 14→16) put the idle figure well under the\n313|limit; I did not locate the STORY-260830-1oqfec 96 s figure on the board and do\n314|not claim it.\n315|\n316|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n317|\n318|1. P1-c: validate non-message payload values (number model + nested\n319|   duplicates, depth) at Build and Decode with the existing walker; negatives\n320|   at both entries for a non-message kind, assert the sealed bytes are never\n321|   rounded/collapsed; narrowing mutant.\n322|2. P2-α: one extension value-fault negative per admission site (16 Decode\n323|   sites + the two payload-level sites), harness rows.\n324|3. P2-β: decode duplicate-entry row for the raw manifest + harness row.\n325|4. P2-γ: refuse duplicate plan keys in `checkPlanItemMatch`; negative +\n326|   narrowing mutant.\n327|5. P3: null-content XOR; the three misreporting messages; rows for\n328|   `input_blocked`, `-(2^53)`, U+2029, payload top-level duplicate, decode\n329|   external-null-parent; `EncodeNativeIdentity` contract; `N-main-count` note;\n330|   dead `sourceBasisObject`; state or cover the census arms in P3-g′.\n331|\n332|Checklist state left by this review: the four reviewer rows (Implementation\n333|matches AC; Solution fits project architecture; Tests green; Gate … attacked,\n334|not read) are unchecked; \"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence\n335|added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\" is checked. Status\n336|routed to `to-dev`.","final_result":true}}}
