{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b144-2d0b-7f30-96a3-e7fabafc632c"},"sequence":459,"recorded_at":1780531400000913,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b145-4baf-7500-95b3-9af4e1a97d83"},"task_id":"01a0b145-4baf-7500-95b3-9af4e1a97d83","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b145-4baf-7500-95b3-9af4e1a97d83","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-24z2b3 Results — implement-clone-bundle-and-canonical-session-types\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n4|worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q`) on base `888ae3d`\n5|(= `origin/main` at handoff; no refresh needed); no commit on the\n6|Story branch. This is attempt 3 (rework rev3 of review\n7|RUN-260917-c05bc8, which routed rev2 CHANGES REQUESTED with two P1,\n8|six P2, eight P3 findings). Every finding is answered below with the\n9|change, the test that fails without it, and the evidence path.\n10|\n11|## Delivered (rev3 delta over rev2)\n12|\n13|`internal/clonebundle` (11 production files) now, over the rev2 tree:\n14|\n15|- Descriptor identity linked to the entry (`blobref.go`,\n16|  `rawmanifest.go`): `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` takes the entry's\n17|  `blob_descriptor_id` and refuses a verified descriptor that is not\n18|  the one the entry names, at both `buildRawEntries` and\n19|  `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors`.\n20|- AX number model + nested-duplicate refusal on extension values\n21|  (`decode.go`): `checkExtensionsClosed` enforces reverse-DNS keys\n22|  (owner) plus recursive value validation (integer literals only,\n23|  |n| <= 2^53-1, no fraction/exponent, duplicate-free at every\n24|  depth, mirroring `canonicaljson.validateAXNumbers`), at every\n25|  Build (`encodeExtensions`) and Decode admission site.\n26|- Environ gate adoption (`decode.go` + call sites): the scalar forks\n27|  are one-line delegating wrappers in the `sessadapter` convention;\n28|  the string measure is characters (`TestMultibyteStringMeasure`).\n29|- Decode-side negatives for every P2-b row, verifier/install\n30|  negatives (P2-c), duplicate-raw-keys refusal (P2-d), identity\n31|  re-decode before hashing (P2-e), content-block XOR (P3-b),\n32|  one-per-plan-candidate refusal at build (P3-c), hardened\n33|  sanitizer with the exact bound stated (P3-a), per-plant harness\n34|  logs (P3-e), LOGBOOK/hygiene fixes (P3-f/g/h).\n35|\n36|## Finding-by-finding table\n37|\n38|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence |\n39||---|---|---|---|\n40|| P1-a descriptor identity unlinked | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` takes `wantDescriptorID` and requires `calculated == want`; both callers pass the entry claim (`blobref.go`, `rawmanifest.go`) | `TestRawManifestRefusals/build/descriptor_id_mismatch`, `TestVerifyRawManifestDescriptorsRefusals` (link row), `TestBlobAgreementRefusals` (identity row) | `mutants/run2/N-descriptor-id-link.log`, `pkg-test.log` |\n41|| P1-b AX number fork | `checkExtensionsClosed` + recursive value walker at all 16 admission sites; `encodeExtensions` validates marshaled values at build | `TestRawManifestRefusals/extension_values/*` (1.5, 2^53, 2^60, exponent, nested, dup incl. resealed) | `mutants/run2/N-extension-number.log`, `mutants/run2/N-extension-nested-dup.log`, `pkg-test.log` |\n42|| P2-a bytes measure | `stringLength` delegates to `environ.StringLength`; every build-side `len()` bound rune-counts (64 KiB inline stays bytes) | `TestMultibyteStringMeasure` (300-char/600-byte admit, 512 admit, 513 refuse) | `pkg-test.log` |\n43|| P2-f environ fork | scalar gates are delegating wrappers; package keeps sanitizer/exclusion/coupling/reconciliation/extension-values only | whole suite (delegation) + `TestMultibyteStringMeasure` | `pkg-test.log` |\n44|| P2-b decode dups (capture items) | negative added (code already refused) | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/decode/items_duplicate_key` | `mutants/run2/N-capture-items-dup-decode.log` |\n45|| P2-b decode dups (digests) | delegating wrapper + negatives at all 3 call sites | `.../decode/parents_duplicate` (killer), `heads_duplicate`, `prints_duplicate` rows | `mutants/run2/N-sorted-digests-dup.log` |\n46|| P2-b decode dups (strings) | delegating wrapper + negatives at both call sites | `.../decode/evidence_reason_codes_duplicate` (killer), `excluded_classes_duplicate` row | `mutants/run2/N-sorted-strings-dup.log` |\n47|| P2-b decode dups (raw_refs) | negative added | `.../decode/evidence_raw_refs_duplicate` | `mutants/run2/N-rawrefs-dup-decode.log` |\n48|| P2-b decode class/actor/status/visibility | negatives added | `item_class_mystery`, `main_with_parent`, `evidence_status_maybe`, `visibility_secret` rows | `mutants/run2/N-decode-*.log` (4 logs) |\n49|| P2-b verify-skip-0 | negative added | `TestVerifyRawManifestDescriptorsRefusals` (entry-0-only wrong bytes) | `mutants/run2/N-verify-descriptors-skip-0.log` |\n50|| P2-b install-site-claim | negative added | `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` (wrong-claim row) | `mutants/run2/N-install-site-claim.log` |\n51|| P2-c verifier positive-only | `TestVerifyRawManifestDescriptorsRefusals` (fetch/absent/wrong/link) | same | `pkg-test.log` |\n52|| P2-c install arms | `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` (claim/short/long); blob_id/size parse arms stated as owner-enforced defense-in-depth in TRACEABILITY.md | same | `pkg-test.log` |\n53|| P2-c N-descriptor-claim note | split into per-site rows `N-descriptor-claim-agreement` + `N-install-site-claim` | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` | both per-plant logs |\n54|| P2-d duplicate raw keys | `deriveRawComplete` returns false; `VerifyCaptureReconciliation` refuses duplicates outright | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` (dup raw/plan rows + derive direct) | `mutants/run2/N-reconcile-rawkeys-dup.log` |\n55|| P2-e IdentityDigest seals undecodable | re-decode before hashing (as `buildCaptureManifest` does) | `TestIdentityDigestRefusals` (bad kind, bad ext key, opaque, session) | `mutants/run2/N-identity-rededecode.log` |\n56|| P3-a sanitizer scope | hardened: `unicode.IsControl` (C1), Cf/Zl/Zp invisible marks, case-folded AX marker, schemeless password-colon; exact bound in code comment + TRACEABILITY.md | `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer` corpus (+U+0085/U+2028/U+200B/URN:AX:/userinfo rows) | `mutants/run2/N-sanitizer-control.log`, `pkg-test.log` |\n57|| P3-b content blocks | XOR enforced: exactly one of content/descriptor | `block_neither_content_nor_descriptor`, `block_both_content_and_descriptor` rows | `mutants/run2/N-block-xor.log` |\n58|| P3-c items != plan sealed | `checkPlanItemMatch` refuses at build; raw-half incompleteness still seals with `raw_complete=false` | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/build_plan_match` (extra/missing/renamed) | `mutants/run2/N-plan-item-match.log` |\n59|| P3-d N-exclusion-config delete | replaced with a true narrowing (admits exactly `settings.bak.3`) | `TestRawManifestExcludesTrustMaterial` | `mutants/run2/N-exclusion-config.log` |\n60|| P3-e verdict-only log | harness `--log-dir` writes one raw log per plant with subprocess exit | harness itself | `mutants/run2/*.log`, `mutants/run3/*.log` (37 logs each) |\n61|| P3-f LOGBOOK sentence | fixed: production calls neither `VerifyObjectIdentity` (only the fixture does); `CalculateObjectIdentity` + local comparisons | text | `LOGBOOK.md` diff |\n62|| P3-g Core nominal | stated in `BoundaryInput` comment + TRACEABILITY.md: real protection is `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | text | `boundary.go`, `TRACEABILITY.md` |\n63|| P3-h dead code | removed `_ = extensionBytes`, `_ = manifest`, `_ = workspace`, `kindOf`, wrong-unit comment |