{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c81b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b144-2d0b-7f30-96a3-e7fabafc632c"},"sequence":616,"recorded_at":1780531400001227,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b145-f79a-7500-b827-f38d2e26aa60"},"task_id":"01a0b145-f79a-7500-b827-f38d2e26aa60","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b145-f79a-7500-b827-f38d2e26aa60","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-19-1\",\n  \"command\": \"WT=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree; git -C \\\"$WT\\\" diff --stat 2>&1; echo \\\"===LOGBOOK diff===\\\"; git -C \\\"$WT\\\" diff LOGBOOK.md 2>&1 | head -40; echo \\\"===README diff===\\\"; git -C \\\"$WT\\\" diff README.md 2>&1 | head -60; echo \\\"===untracked===\\\"; git -C \\\"$WT\\\" status --short 2>&1; echo \\\"===clonebundle ls===\\\"; ls -la \\\"$WT/internal/clonebundle/\\\" \\\"$WT/internal/clonebundle/testdata/\\\" 2>&1\",\n  \"description\": \"Record pre-existing candidate changes\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \" LOGBOOK.md |  9 +++++++++\\n README.md  | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+)\\n===LOGBOOK diff===\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 43c6d21..bd961c0 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,15 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-17\\n \\n+### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n+\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n+- OWNERSHIP: `canonicaljson` keeps its `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows (that table's census pins every row); this package is the validating owner and reuses `Canonicalize` (byte transform), `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons (blobs; never the attesting `VerifyObjectIdentity` entry — only the test fixture calls it — per the provhost no-attestation bound), `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, the `environ` scalar gate set via delegating wrappers, `scalar`, `hosttrust`, and `localstore.PutBlob`. No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (83.9% statements), 36 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` + `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` prove the localstore delegation (double install agrees; forged claim, short/long/tampered bytes refuse); durability itself is the landed localstore discipline (purity bound for this package: no second write path). README package section added with test commands and no capability claim.\\n+- REV3 (rework of review RUN-260917-c05bc8): P1-a descriptor identity linked to the entry at build + evidence verification; P1-b AX number model + nested-duplicate refusal on extension values at build + decode; P2-f/P2-a environ gate adoption with the character string measure; P2-b/P2-c decode-side negatives for every surviving row + verifier/install negatives with per-plant logs; P2-d duplicate raw keys refused; P2-e identity re-decode before hashing; P3-b content XOR enforced; P3-c one-per-plan-candidate refused at build; P3-a sanitizer hardened with the exact bound stated; P3-d/P3-e harness rows fixed; P3-f/g/h hygiene. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n+- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): per-kind event payload fact registries past the envelope (incl. non-message payload numbers); `maximal_safe` planning past the refusal gate; G2 admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`; Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- AC: 18 of 18 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n+\\n ### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n - DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n - F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n===README diff===\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 1f8fc60..ca5639e 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2383,6 +2383,33 @@ go test ./internal/matjournal -count=1 -cover\\n python3 internal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py\\n ```\\n \\n+## Clone Bundle and Canonical Session Types\\n+\\n+[`internal/clonebundle`](internal/clonebundle) validates and constructs\\n+the Section 13.14.1 clone capture contracts: Clone Raw Object Manifest\\n+1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 with its Capture Items, Capture\\n+Source Basis, and Capture Boundary, Canonical Session 1.0.0 with its\\n+Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 with Source Evidence and raw byte-range\\n+references, the NativeIdentity and WorkspaceBinding identities, and\\n+immutable source generations. Every Build entry produces byte-identical\\n+canonical bytes for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the\\n+closed shape, the class vocabularies, the included/excluded content\\n+rule, the core-derived `raw_complete` reconciliation, the stable-proof\\n+coupling, and the row-21 hosttrust exclusion allowlist. Blob Descriptor\\n+identity and byte-count agreement verify through `canonicaljson`, and\\n+blob bytes install only through the `localstore` no-replace discipline;\\n+the package performs no durable write itself. The clause map in\\n+[`internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md)\\n+maps every pinned clause to its production entry and test, with the\\n+sibling-owned bounds stated. It adds no `ax` command, no `doctor`\\n+result, and no runtime capability claim.\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1 -cover\\n+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py\\n+```\\n+\\n ## Crash/Restart Outcome Gate\\n \\n [`internal/crashgate`](internal/crashgate) executes the Section 13.13\\n===untracked===\\n M LOGBOOK.md\\n M README.md\