{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c905","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b144-2d0b-7f30-96a3-e7fabafc632c"},"sequence":733,"recorded_at":1780531400001461,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b147-4e05-7501-ab95-4cd3478fe28e"},"task_id":"01a0b147-4e05-7501-ab95-4cd3478fe28e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b147-4e05-7501-ab95-4cd3478fe28e","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-24-1\",\n  \"command\": \"WT=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree; git -C \\\"$WT\\\" diff 888ae3dff6a55c29bfaf311957748d405ed1ab06 -- README.md 2>&1 | head -50; echo \\\"===NEW HEAD LOGBOOK head===\\\"; git -C \\\"$WT\\\" show HEAD:LOGBOOK.md 2>&1 | head -25\",\n  \"description\": \"Show README diff and new trunk LOGBOOK\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 1f8fc60..ca5639e 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2383,6 +2383,33 @@ go test ./internal/matjournal -count=1 -cover\\n python3 internal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py\\n ```\\n \\n+## Clone Bundle and Canonical Session Types\\n+\\n+[`internal/clonebundle`](internal/clonebundle) validates and constructs\\n+the Section 13.14.1 clone capture contracts: Clone Raw Object Manifest\\n+1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 with its Capture Items, Capture\\n+Source Basis, and Capture Boundary, Canonical Session 1.0.0 with its\\n+Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 with Source Evidence and raw byte-range\\n+references, the NativeIdentity and WorkspaceBinding identities, and\\n+immutable source generations. Every Build entry produces byte-identical\\n+canonical bytes for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the\\n+closed shape, the class vocabularies, the included/excluded content\\n+rule, the core-derived `raw_complete` reconciliation, the stable-proof\\n+coupling, and the row-21 hosttrust exclusion allowlist. Blob Descriptor\\n+identity and byte-count agreement verify through `canonicaljson`, and\\n+blob bytes install only through the `localstore` no-replace discipline;\\n+the package performs no durable write itself. The clause map in\\n+[`internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md)\\n+maps every pinned clause to its production entry and test, with the\\n+sibling-owned bounds stated. It adds no `ax` command, no `doctor`\\n+result, and no runtime capability claim.\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1 -cover\\n+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py\\n+```\\n+\\n ## Crash/Restart Outcome Gate\\n \\n [`internal/crashgate`](internal/crashgate) executes the Section 13.13\\n===NEW HEAD LOGBOOK head===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260917-10k118: reconstructed the reviewed v0.7.0 adoption on trunk 7efe385 (STORY-260916-3uqbwq unlandable, accepted CRs frozen)\\n- METHOD: true pin delta is `git diff e4e3e88 9cb5dd4` (10 files) — the exported 238-file patch diffs unrelated tips and would revert five landed stories, so it was used as transport only; rev3 candidate bytes applied (15 modified + 3 new) with the 5 trunk-merged files copied verbatim after diff-review (no trunk test lost, `task-board.config.json` untouched). All 19 machine-applied files `cmp`-identical to the rev3 bytes; ownership sha256 `2548870d…8a5070`, projection digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6` recomputed two independent ways.\\n- RE-VERIFIED (this session, fresh clone + production helpers): tag `d4abe46f…795b3` Good, peeled `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes sha256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` byte-identical to `SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; lock 64/64 rows order- and set-identical to the §1.5 table (1 known order normalization); 65/65 bindings + 132/132 cases carried with 3 reviewed additions each; all 49 discharged clauses re-measured (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392, excerpts verbatim); rev3 prose says \\\"48 carried clause lines\\\" in two places — measured 49, matching the 49/569 numerator; artifact is right, prose miscounted.\\n- FINDING F1: the reviewed v0.7.0 source normative-section group keeps production `VerifyV060` while its cases moved to the v0.7.0 pair; the v0.5.0→v0.6.0 precedent moved `Verify`→`VerifyV060`, so the pattern says `VerifyV070`. Green because the gate checks declaration existence only. Reviewed bytes are not rewritten in a reconstruction; the new re-derivation test pins the carried reference literally with the rationale.\\n- NEW TESTS (this Story's scope): `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (carry completeness, clause re-measurement via production inventory+quote, no self-minted claims) and `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport` (fenced line byte-equal to tool output, 8 headline prose figures re-derived). Narrowing mutants per test + token-preserving README plant with full behavioral suites; harmless controls SURVIVED. Full 27-command suite green on the exact tree.\\n- FIGURES: contracts=64, acceptance cases=135, bindings=68, clauses 49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim.\\n- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n\\n### TASK-260916-n9r71p: bound v0.7.0 launch-plan catalog row and curator story owners\\n- AUTHORITY: catalogue generation, Current, CI roots and traceability consume the adopted v0.7.0 lock/document/inventory; four release projections preserve V060/V050/V043 history. Metadata digest `c4094101…50274a35`; ownership digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6`. Localstore stays on explicit CurrentV050. Validation command 22 is the release-agnostic `-adopted` gate, which resolves to the v0.7.0 metadata/lock pair on this tree.\\n- DELTA: +Launch Plan request `urn:ax:schema:launch-plan-request` 1.0.0 (64th row, census-only, no catalog family); provider families carry the 2.1.0/3.1.0 minors (SPEC 7.5 adds members not operations; consumers range over names); session-record 3.1.0, error 1.4.0/1.5.0 and manifest/probe 1.1.0 stay census-only (carrying 3.1.0 panics canonicaljson init — no Go shape validator yet — same init-panic rationale as error 1.4.0). +3 section bindings (13.1, 13.10, 14.1), +1 fixture (`pin:ax-launch-plan-request-v1`), gaps updated for 5.1/7.3/7.4/7.5/appendix-d with story owners; 48 carried clause lines re-measured against SPEC.v0.7.0.md (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392 shifts, every excerpt verbatim, no ID shifts).\\n- OWNERS: all 7 launch-plan clause areas name implementing EPIC-260916-18uelk stories with unevidenced coverage — 3fjjtn parsing/refusals (14.1, 13.1, contract), 2q85nu record embedding (5.1), 1kp1lx stdin/replay (7.5), 1ea7od plugin capability (7.3/7.4), 3aukw3 drift (13.10), 3ustb3 naming (13.1 split), vucwn0 vectors (fixture, appendix-d split). The source-derived AdoptedSections test requires 6/6 plus 2 split attributions and refuses each through VerifyAssignedSections.\\n- HISTORY: registry re-derived from the trunk-final v0.6.0 registry, carrying the five landed stories' 31 acceptance cases and 9 section bindings (2.2, 2.4, 5.3/5.4/5.5, 6.6, 7.7, 8, 10.6, 11.10.1–4, 13.12/13.13, 16.1) with re-measured clause lines; v0.6.0/v0.5.0 locks, registries, readers and historical tests byte-untouched versus trunk; the v0.7.0 inventory is identifier-equal to v0.6.0 (170 ids, same digest), so legacy verification derives both historical registries from the adopted lock. P3 closed: pin.go/specdoc.go consumer comments now true in the present tense; section:11.10.5 carried as a Disclosure owner (source evidence only, no implementation claim).\\n- FIGURES: contracts=64, normative section keys=36, acceptance cases=135, fixtures=33, historical contracts=55; bindings=68 (full=2, partial=6, sliver=4, unevidenced=52, unmeasured=4), unowned=7, discharged clauses=49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim anywhere.\\n- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8050,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2013,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
