{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd31","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b144-2d0b-7f30-96a3-e7fabafc632c"},"sequence":1267,"recorded_at":1780531400002529,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"96a3132b-8530-4e47-8657-36d15f2da569"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b14a-8442-7f31-8bb5-3d0a7cba453d"},"task_id":"01a0b14a-8442-7f31-8bb5-3d0a7cba453d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b14a-8442-7f31-8bb5-3d0a7cba453d","chunk":"Read text file `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Clone Bundle Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-24z2b3)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/clonebundle`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1.\n5|The Story's FINAL leaf carries the `internal/traceability` registry\n6|bindings and re-pin; this file is the first-leaf clause record.\n7|\n8|## Why this package validates instead of canonicaljson\n9|\n10|The `canonicaljson` closed-shape registry keeps\n11|`rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows for\n12|`clone-raw-object-manifest`, `clone-capture-manifest`,\n13|`canonical-session`, and `canonical-event` 1.0.0, and that table's\n14|census pins every row. Replacing them would fork shape ownership, so\n15|this package is the validating owner: it reuses\n16|`canonicaljson.Canonicalize` (byte transform),\n17|`canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons\n18|(Blob Descriptors; never the attesting entry, per the provhost\n19|no-attestation bound),\n20|`sessadapter.DecodeTuple` (Environment Tuples),\n21|the `environ` scalar gate set (`CheckStringBounds`,\n22|`CheckUint53Bounds`, `CheckDigest`, `CheckUUIDv7`,\n23|`CheckTimestamp`, `CheckSortedUniqueStrings`,\n24|`CheckSortedUniqueDigests`, `CheckExtensions`, `StringLength`,\n25|`DecodeStrictObject`) through one-line delegating wrappers in the\n26|`sessadapter` convention, keeping only package-specific rules\n27|(sanitizer, exclusion, coupling, reconciliation, extension values),\n28|`scalar` (digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, paths),\n29|`hosttrust` (row-21 exclusion matchers), and\n30|`localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob` (blob install). No rule is\n31|reimplemented where a landed owner exists.\n32|\n33|## Clause map\n34|\n35|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n36||---|---|---|\n37|| 13.14.1 Raw Manifest closed envelope + self ID | `BuildRawObjectManifest`, `DecodeRawObjectManifest` | `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestRawManifestRefusals/decode` |\n38|| 13.14.1 RawObjectEntry class subset (no credential/auth/runtime/lock) | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals/build` (5 class rows) |\n39|| 13.14.1 sorted unique entries, total_bytes sum | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals` (unsorted, duplicate, total mismatch) |\n40|| 13.14.1 sanitized native key, never an AX Session ID | `SanitizeNativeKey` | `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer`, raw/capture/session/event refusal rows |\n41|| Sanitizer exact bound (pinned text leaves scope open) | `SanitizeNativeKey` | `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer` corpus: refuses Cc+C1 controls, Cf/Zl/Zp invisible format marks, absolute paths, UUIDv7, password-colon-before-@ (schemed or schemeless), case-folded `urn:ax:`; admits spaces, bare `@`, bare `:` |\n42|| Row 21 exclusion allowlist at construction | `refuseExcludedMember` | `TestRawManifestExcludesTrustMaterial`, `TestCaptureManifestExcludesTrustMaterial` |\n43|| 13.14.1 CaptureItem 9-class vocabulary | `ValidCaptureClass`, `buildCaptureItem`, `decodeCaptureItem` | `TestCaptureClassVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestCaptureItemRefusals` |\n44|| 13.14.1 included/excluded content rule | `checkItemDisposition` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (6 content rows) |\n45|| 13.14.1 always-excluded classes never included | `alwaysExcludedClass` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (4 class rows) |\n46|| 13.14.1 exact excluded_classes | `excludedRowClasses`, `excludedClassesExact` | `TestExcludedClassesExactGate`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/decode` |\n47|| 13.14.1 core-derived raw_complete + reconciliation | `deriveRawComplete`, `VerifyCaptureReconciliation` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n48|| 13.14.1 unknown blocks maximal_safe | `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n49|| 13.14.1 Capture Source Basis union | `DecodeSourceBasis`, `buildSourceBasis` | `TestSourceBasisRefusals` |\n50|| 13.14.1 Capture Boundary union, stable proof coupling | `DecodeCaptureBoundary`, `buildBoundary`, `checkProofCoupling` | `TestBoundaryRefusals`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n51|| 13.14.1 unstable is core-created, G2 rejects | `buildBoundary` (Core), `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestBoundaryRefusals/build_core-only_unstable`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n52|| 13.14.1 NativeIdentity closed shape | `DecodeNativeIdentity`, `EncodeNativeIdentity` | `TestNativeIdentityRoundTrip`, `TestIdentityRefusals/native_identity` |\n53|| 13.14.1 source_identity_digest terminal digest | `IdentityDigest` | `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip` |\n54|| 13.14.1 WorkspaceBinding closed shape, normalized cwd | `DecodeWorkspaceBinding`, `checkCwdRelative` | `TestIdentityRefusals/workspace_binding` |\n55|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session + Actor rules | `BuildCanonicalSession`, `DecodeCanonicalSession` | `TestBuildCanonicalSessionRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals` |\n56|| 13.14.1 Canonical Event envelope + 26 kinds + visibility | `BuildCanonicalEvent`, `DecodeCanonicalEvent`, `ValidEventKind` | `TestEventKindVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals` |\n57|| 13.14.1 SourceEvidence + RawReference + synthesized coupling | `DecodeSourceEvidence`, `buildSourceEvidence`, `checkEvidenceCoupling` | `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/evidence` |\n58|| 13.14.1 message-like content blocks, 64 KiB inline bound | `checkPayload`, `checkContentBlocks` | `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` (block rows + 64 KiB boundary) |\n59|| 13.14.1 contiguous ordinals from zero | `CheckOrdinalContiguity` | `TestOrdinalContiguity` |\n60|| 13.14.1 immutable generations | `ParseGeneration`, `Generation.Equal`, `CheckDigestsEqual` | `TestGenerationRefusals`, `TestBoundaryRefusals` |\n61|| 13.14.1 reverse-DNS extensions, no normative reference | `encodeExtensions`, `checkExtensionsClosed` | contract round trips + `bad extensions` rows in every refusal table |\n62|| 1.6 AX number model + nested duplicate refusal on extension values | `checkExtensionsClosed`, `checkExtensionValues`, `checkAXNumberLiteral` | `TestRawManifestRefusals/extension_values` (1.5, 2^53, 2^60, exponent, nested float/unsafe, nested duplicate incl. resealed) |\n63|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `stringLength` via `environ` | `TestMultibyteStringMeasure` (300-char/600-byte admit, 512 admit, 513 refuse) |\n64|| 13.14.1 one item per plan candidate at construction | `checkPlanItemMatch` | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/build_plan_match` (extra, missing, renamed candidate) |\n65|| 13.14.1 content block inline-XOR-descriptor | `checkContentBlocks` | `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` (neither, both) |\n66|| 13.14.1 duplicate raw keys refused | `VerifyCaptureReconciliation`, `deriveRawComplete` | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` (duplicate raw/plan keys, derive direct) |\n67|| 13.14.1 source_identity_digest over sanitized bytes | `IdentityDigest` (re-decodes before hashing) | `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestIdentityDigestRefusals` (bad kind, bad extension key, unsanitized opaque/session) |\n68|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor identity + byte-count agreement | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` (with entry identity link) | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestVerifyRawManifestDescriptorsRefusals` |\n69|| 10.2 entry names the verified descriptor | `buildRawEntries`, `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` | build `descriptor id mismatch` row, `TestVerifyRawManifestDescriptorsRefusals` (fetch/absent/wrong/link) |\n70|| 10.2 no-replace install (fsync + verify + atomic) | `InstallRawBlob` via `localstore.PutBlob` | `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent`, `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` (forged claim, short/long bytes) |\n71|| 7.8 tuple/probe/manifest/discover/inspect reuse | `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` at every `source_environment` | `bad tuple` rows in raw/capture/session/event tables |\n72|| Byte-identical construction | all Build entries | `RoundTrip` tests rebuild and compare bytes |\n73|\n74|## Durability bound\n75|\n76|This package performs no durable write: `InstallRawBlob` delegates\n77|every byte to `localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob` (no-replace install,\n78|fsync, size/digest verification, quarantine on collision). The\n79|landed crash/idempotency evidence for that discipline lives with\n80|`internal/localstore` (`object_store_test.go`,\n81|`object_store_fault_unix_test.go`, projection fault suites);\n82|`TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` proves the delegation end to end\n83|(double install agrees, tampered bytes refuse). No second write\n84|path exists in this package.\n85|\n86|## Stated bounds (sibling scope)\n87|\n88|- Non-message Canonical Event payload member values past the\n89|  envelope: `checkPayload` enforces strict objects and content-block\n90|  rules, but per-kind fact values (including their numbers) are the\n91|  normalization sibling's registry. Only `extensions` members carry\n92|  the AX value model here.\n93|- `-0` and leading-`+`/leading-zero integer literals in extension\n94|  values admit, exactly as `canonicaljson.validateAXNumbers`\n95|  admits them (`strconv.ParseInt` parity); the model refuses\n96|  fractions, exponents, and magnitudes at or beyond 2^53.\n97|- `BoundaryInput.Core` is caller-asserted; the real unstable-archive\n98|  protection is `RefuseUnstableForTarget` at target admission.\n99|- `InstallRawBlob`'s `blob_id`/`size` member-parse arms repeat the\n100|  owner grammar after `CalculateObjectIdentity` already enforced\n101|  it (`validateBlobDescriptor` requires digest `blob_id` and uint53\n102|  `size`): defense in depth, unreachable on failure, pinned by the\n103|  owner suite; the install negatives pin the claim comparison and\n104|  the store size/digest enforcement end to end.\n105|- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries beyond the\n106|  Section 13.14.1 envelope enforced in `checkPayload` (normalization\n107|  sibling).\n108|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n109|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n110|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n111|- Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize operation wiring\n112|  (stays owned by `sessadapter`); this package owns the contracts\n113|  those operations produce, not the operation frames.\n114|- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\n115|  (Story FINAL leaf).","final_result":true}}}
